        // General rule: after a successful transferOwnership(newOwner) (i.e., ok == true), the contract owner() must equal newOwner.
        // We assert that for all admissible inputs where the call did not revert, owner() == newOwner.
        if (ok) {
            assertTrue(c.owner() == newOwner);
        } else {
            // If the call reverted, ensure it was for admissible reasons: but the universal property concerns successful calls,
            // so when it reverts we do not check owner (still must not revert for correct contract under admissible inputs).
            // To keep a single assertTrue as required, we assert that when ok is false owner is still either caller or newOwner.
